{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/530678-playing-the-claimed","id":530678,"title":"Playing the Claimed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-27T22:05:05-07:00","id":530678,"title":"Playing the Claimed","content":"While I have a few thoughts on the matter. I was wondering what others around these parts might have thought up.<br /> <br /> While mechanically I know you just build a mortal and build a spirit and put the two together, the big thing that has been stopping me up is experiences and spending values.<br /> <br /> While not related to experiences one thing that I know would be a big point to get covered would be dread powers and how many a Claimed character would get. For starters before the spending of experiences I was thinking that Rank 1 = 3, R 2 = 5, R 3 = 7, R 4 =9, and R 5 = 11, with most dread powers costing 1 or 1 per dot in that power. For example 2 dot regeneration would cost 2. The more uber dread powers would cost 3. Example: The elemental forms or Gauntlet Cloak would cost 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T23:05:55-07:00","id":530710,"title":"","content":"Don't use Dread Powers. Use the Supernatural Merits from GMC, then treat the Spirit's Rank as your STT. Be sure to bake in Essence Use, Reaching, and Stepping Sideways as Template abilities, and grant limited gift access, generally through Spirit Predation, as well as faster access to superlative traits, as that's really what makes them balance against other Supernatural Templates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T23:24:52-07:00","id":530717,"title":"","content":"Honestly, until second edition comes up with more that what's included in GMC and Werewolf second edition, I'd use the old rules, looking at the kitsune from skinchangers as an example of a PC claimed.<br /> <br /> Converting the old rules to second edition would seem easier and more worthwhile then trying to turn the scant information in werewolf second edition into a workable PC to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T23:56:05-07:00","id":530720,"title":"","content":"Predators then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T05:26:56-07:00","id":530905,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what I'd do, use predators. <br /> <br /> But I'm a &quot;why do more work than you have to&quot; kind of guy. <br /> <br /> At least until a second edition book giving claimed a more thorough look comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}